  "question": {
    "text": "Consider two identical galvanometers and two identical resistors with resistance R. If the internal resistance of the galvanometers <math><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> which of the following statement(s) about any one of the galvanometers<br />is(are) true ?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "The maximum voltage range is obtained when all the components are connected in series",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The maximum voltage range is obtained when the two resistors and one galvanometer are connected in series, and the second galvanometer is connected in parallel to the first galvanometer",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The maximum current range is obtained when all the components are connected in parallel",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The maximum current range is obtained when the two galvanometers are connected in series and the combination is connected in parallel with both the resistors.",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B",
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
